Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not take venlafaxine if you are allergic to venlafaxine or to desvenlafaxine (Pristiq).
Do not use venlafaxine if you have used an MAO inhibitor in the past 14 days.
A dangerous drug interaction could occur.
MAO inhibitors include isocarboxazid, linezolid, methylene blue injection, phenelzine, and tranylcypromine.
Tell your doctor if you also use stimulant medicine, opioid medicine, herbal products, or medicine for depression, mental illness, Parkinson's disease, migraine headaches, serious infections, or prevention of nausea and vomiting.
An interaction with venlafaxine could cause a serious condition called serotonin syndrome.
To make sure venlafaxine is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have ever had:
bipolar disorder (manic depression);
heart disease, high blood pressure, high cholesterol or triglycerides, or a stroke;
diabetes;
lung disease;
glaucoma;
a thyroid disorder;
a seizure;
sexual problems;
bleeding problems;
low blood levels of sodium; or
liver or kidney disease.
Triplet: ["venlafaxine", "has contraindication", "kidney disease"]

The relation 'has contraindication' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug should not be used by patients who have the condition specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'contraindicated in': The subject drug should not be used by patients who have the condition or characteristic specified by the object entity.
B. 'not a substitute for': The subject drug should not be used in place of the medical device or medication specified by the object entity.
C. 'should be avoided with': Patients taking the subject drug should avoid the substance or activity specified by the object entity.
D. 'not used for': The subject drug is not indicated or used for the condition, situation, or purpose specified by the object entity.
E. 'not approved for': The subject drug is not approved or not recommended for use in the patient population specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
